<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basorun Gaa crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1745–<a href="/years/1774">1774</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basorun-gaa">Basorun Gaa</a> crisis was the period of c. 1745–1774 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basorun">Basorun</a> Gaa, head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-mesi">Oyo Mesi</a> council, dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafins</a> were compelled to die. It revealed the dangerous imbalance between royal and council power in Oyo. It ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abiodun">Alaafin Abiodun</a> overthrew and executed Gaa, but the instability foreshadowed Oyo's decline.</p></div>
